{"from": "claim:lk-06-twelve-named", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-10-02-04-names-of-the-twelve", "note": "Luke's list has Judas son of James where Matthew 10:3 and Mark 3:18 have Thaddaeus; Luke omits Matthew's epithet 'the tax collector' and Mark's 'Boanerges'."}
{"from": "person:judas-son-of-james", "type": "related_to", "to": "person:thaddaeus", "note": "Luke 6:16 names Judas (not Iscariot) as son of James where Matthew/Mark name Thaddaeus; the traditional identification of the two as one apostle is not made by Luke."}
{"from": "claim:lk-06-level-place", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-05-01-taught-on-mountain", "note": "Luke's sermon is given standing on a level place (topos pedinos) after coming down from the mountain; Matthew's is taught on a mountain - the Sermon on the Plain against the Sermon on the Mount."}
{"from": "claim:lk-06-level-place", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mk-03-08-crowds-from-idumea-tyre-sidon", "note": "The same regional catchment of followers (Judea, Jerusalem, around Tyre and Sidon) as Mark 3:7-8, at a different occasion."}
{"from": "claim:lk-06-save-life-sabbath", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-12-10-sabbath-healing-debate", "note": "Luke words the Sabbath question as 'to do good or to do harm, to save a life or to kill'; Matthew as 'is it lawful to heal on the Sabbath?'"}
{"from": "claim:lk-06-blessed-poor", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:lk-06-woes", "note": "Luke pairs blessings on the poor/hungry/weeping with woes on the rich/full/laughing; Matthew has the blessings without the woes."}
