{"from": "text:mishnah-yoma-8-6", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-06-save-life-sabbath", "grade": "C", "note": "'A case of uncertainty concerning a life-threatening situation overrides Shabbat' - the life-over-Sabbath principle inside the same legal culture that asks whether it is lawful to save a life on the Sabbath; redacted c. 200 CE, so it may not describe the practice of the 30s CE exactly."}
{"from": "text:4q521-2", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-06-blessed-poor", "grade": "C", "note": "A pre-Christian Qumran text expects the coming age to bring 'he will proclaim good news to the poor... enrich the hungry' - the expectation that the poor are blessed in God's kingdom; it attests the expectation, not the saying or the sermon."}
